WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:02.090
- I wanna close that with something fun.

00:00:02.090 --> 00:00:03.356
This is "#What I'm Liking."

00:00:03.356 --> 00:00:06.250
(big band music)
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:08.550
Last year, we hooked up
with a hip hop violinist

00:00:08.550 --> 00:00:11.410
who had a special relationship
with the beluga whales

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.580
at the Mystic Aquarium in Connecticut.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.680
He'd come by to perform for the
sea life. That's super cool.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.910
Now, I wanna share another
special relationship

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:20.280
happening at the aquarium.

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.220
This is between a trainer
Courtney and Clara the sea lion

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:28.070
- Clara is a seven year old sea lion,

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.880
and she was rescued years ago

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:33.450
and has been here for
the majority of her life.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.200
Now she just gave you a inside scoop

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.770
on highlighting the very close
relationship that we have.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:40.804
Right, Peanut?

00:00:40.804 --> 00:00:41.792
(Courtney laughs)
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:41.792 --> 00:00:42.625
- My gosh.

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:45.920
That's how I hug people.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.600
I just like lean in and lay on them.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.160
(laughing) That would be awesome.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.260
We've got Courtney and
Clara on the line right now.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:53.957
Courtney watches on
NBC Connecticut at two.

00:00:53.957 --> 00:00:55.670
What's up.
(audience claps and cheers)

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:57.013
Great to meet you.

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:01.480
Oh, my gosh.
- [Audience] Aww.

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:04.520
So how did your tight-knit
relationship with Clara began?

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.410
Begin. What?
(audience laughs)

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:08.220
- So Clara is seven years old,

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.670
but she was rescued off
the coast of California

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.780
when she was under a year old.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:15.710
The United States government
deemed her non- releasable,

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.430
which means that they'll
find her a permanent home

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.536
where she can be an
ambassador for her species.

00:01:21.536 --> 00:01:24.630
Now, the number one reason
why we train our animals

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.660
under our care is for their husbandry

00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:28.420
or their health behaviors.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.740
So having Clara come and sit in my lap

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:34.880
or lay her head on my
shoulder is really important

00:01:34.880 --> 00:01:37.020
because it highlights
the trust that we have,

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:40.370
and it translates for those
important health behaviors

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:44.252
such as voluntary
ultrasounds and radiographs.

00:01:44.252 --> 00:01:46.930
(audience claps)
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:48.570
This is adorable.

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.930
So she's also quite the
performer, right, at the aquarium?

00:01:51.930 --> 00:01:55.140
- She is. So Clara participates
in our current show

00:01:55.140 --> 00:01:57.340
called "Connecting with Conservation,"

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.990
where the whole point of it
is try and inspire guests

00:01:59.990 --> 00:02:02.859
to lead and participate in the three R's

00:02:02.859 --> 00:02:06.010
such as reducing, reusing, and recycling.

00:02:06.010 --> 00:02:08.810
Now, Clara not only does
those behaviors during shows

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.560
but she also shows them outside.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.500
So we're gonna see if she can show you

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.787
her fun vocal (indistinct).

00:02:16.036 --> 00:02:17.070
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.690
Or, can you show your dance moves?

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:20.387
- [Kelly] ♪ Get down, get down ♪

00:02:20.387 --> 00:02:24.142
(laughing) Oh, my gosh.
(audience claps)

00:02:24.142 --> 00:02:28.910
- Can you smile for them?
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:02:28.910 --> 00:02:31.450
- Thank you so much, Courtney and Clara.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.290
Great job, Clara.
(audience claps and cheers)

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.550
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.410
And that's not all, our
season-long partner,

00:02:37.410 --> 00:02:39.920
Pilot Pin Makers of Friction,
the go-to race bull pin

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.380
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show,"
want to celebrate those

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:45.080
creating fearlessly and
just being rad like Clara.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:47.100
So they're gonna give the Ocean Society

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.478
at the Mystic Aquarium $1000.

00:02:49.478 --> 00:02:54.478
(audience claps and cheers)
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:54.563 --> 00:02:55.590
Oh, my God.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.650
I love Clara. Oh, my gosh.

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:00.350
Thank you so much, Courtney,
y'all have a blessed day.

